  BCHN `src/secp256k1/src/modules/schnorr/tests_impl.h`, function `run_schnorr_compact_test`
  (5 cases asserted to VERIFY, 8 asserted to FAIL). These are the vendored fork's own compact
  test vectors for `secp256k1_schnorr_verify` — the exact function this binding calls — so the
  expected answers are independent of LeanBCH entirely.

  The remaining cases are derived mechanically from those: one-bit corruptions of each of the 5
  positive vectors (in the signature, the pubkey, and the digest), which must all FAIL, plus
  length-discipline probes of `CPubKey::GetLen` / the 64-byte Schnorr rule.

  This runs at the EXECUTABLE level, never in the elaborator — the 313 build-time KATs stay
  FFI-free (see LeanBCH/Crypto/Native.lean). Build: `ffi/build.sh && lake build sigkat`.
-/
